cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "SomnoFuse: Multimodal Machine Learning for Sleep Arousal Detection"
authors:
  - family-names: "Arun-Seb"
    given-names: ""
repository-code: "https://github.com/Arun-Seb/SomnoFuse-"
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2025-01-01"
abstract: >
  SomnoFuse is a multimodal machine learning pipeline for sleep arousal
  detection, fusing snoring acoustics (MFCCs, Mel-spectrogram), EEG band
  powers, HRV, SpO2, and respiratory features from polysomnographic
  recordings. Built on the PhysioNet CPS dataset (113 patients, 36 signal
  channels, 81 annotated event types).
keywords:
  - sleep
  - polysomnography
  - multimodal-learning
  - snoring
  - deep-learning
  - pytorch
  - eeg
  - biosignals
  - arousal-detection
references:
  - type: dataset
    title: "Comprehensive Polysomnography (CPS) Dataset"
